# .trivyignore — per-module Trivy suppressions (Issue #2004)
#
# Suppress a CVE only with a documented rationale and (for non-permanent cases)
# an expiry. Format — comment block + the CVE id on its own LAST line:
#
#   # CVE-YYYY-NNNNN — <package:version>
#   # Reason: <why not exploitable / why no fix yet>
#   # Re-evaluate by <month YYYY> or when <dep> is upgraded
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#
# Rules: exp: is mandatory for temporary suppressions (max ~90 days); permanent
# false positives may omit it. Never suppress without a reason (rejected in review).



